# The kit `spell` (checked out at `~/www/spell`) tracks its own code (src/, tests/, bin/, scripts/), the house style
# (agents/), and the glue (package.json, yarn.lock, .yarnrc.yml, repos.json5, tools/):
# every child repo is its own git repo, cloned inside it by `yarn clone`, and ignored here.
/spell-*/
# the two data folders (epic repo-split J5):  the content repo (its own git repo, local only) and your projects (a plain
# folder)
/spell.epics
/spell.spaces

node_modules
.yarn/install-state.gz
.DS_Store
.vitest/
*.log
*.code-workspace
# `/park`'s note on where parked work stopped:  never committed
PARKED-*.md
# the page server's records, at its root:  the kit's since epic repo-split P16 (its pid file, the app's editor's);  its
# logs are `*.log`
.spell-server.json
.spell-server.*.json
# the MAIN checkout's marker:  worktree windows hide its folder's files (spell-epic's window script)
/.spell-main

# the declarations the kit builds for the repos above it (`spell-types`, epic repo-split I12):  never committed
dist-types/


# `spell publish`'s packed packages and their staging folders (epic repo-split P19):  never committed
/dist-packs/

# Claude Code's own worktrees (an agent's isolated copy):  never the kit's files
/.claude/worktrees/
